iguration-change command or every durable FSM implementation.\",\n    \"target_id\": \"963549955e6040b89509dc7d67e601a2\",\n    \"version\": 1,\n    \"source_ids\": [\n     \"src-configstore-contract\",\n     \"src-batchingfsm-contract\",\n     \"src-runfsm\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"resolution_basis\": {},\n  \"prior_review_ids\": [],\n  \"parent_issue_id\": null,\n  \"challenged_components\": [],\n  \"id\": \"4d0f3c6b9af143cdbf76a138eabd8f6c\",\n  \"review_id\": \"input:963549955e6040b89509dc7d67e601a2\",\n  \"target_id\": \"963549955e6040b89509dc7d67e601a2\",\n  \"target_version\": 1,\n  \"aspect\": \"applicability\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n   \"src-configstore-contract\",\n   \"src-batchingfsm-contract\",\n   \"src-runfsm\"\n  ],\n  \"explanation\": \"The check observes the bootstrap configuration entry in one single-node cluster; it does not enumerate every configuration-change command or every durable FSM implementation.\",\n  \"disposition\": \"investigation\",\n  \"reason\": \"Fixed input counterevidence needs an attributed resolution\",\n  \"resolved_by\": null,\n  \"resolution_checks\": []\n }\n]\n==== semantic_reviews\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"6d1fae55a5ff43a4b5fd78eadc0cb443\",\n  \"task_id\": \"review:1c4aa40cf57c4558bd05b3912457343b\",\n  \"check_id\": \"1c4aa40cf57c4558bd05b3912457343b\",\n  \"target_versions\": {\n   \"4d6db0cc9a4b4879b86886aeead58c33\": 1\n  },\n  \"material_ids\": [\n   \"src-api-verifyleader\",\n   \"src-suffrage\",\n   \"src-verifyleader\",\n   \"src-vote\",\n   \"src-notifyall\",\n   \"src-heartbeat\",\n   \"src-startstop\",\n   \"src-quorum\",\n   \"src-lease\"\n  ],\n  \"items\": [\n   {\n    \"target_id\": \"4d6db0cc9a4b4879b86886aeead58c33\",\n    \"aspect\": \"checker_correspondence\",\n    \"status\": \"no_issue_found\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n     \"src-api-verifyleader\",\n     \"src-suffrage\",\n     \"src-verifyleader\",\n     \"src-vote\",\n     \"src-notifyall\",\n     \"src-heartbeat\",\n     \"src-startstop\",\n     \"src-quorum\",\n     \"src-lease\"\n    ],\n    \"rationale\": \"The obligation is sourced by src-api-verifyleader, which documents VerifyLeader as a guard against returning stale data after leadership is lost, and by src-suffrage, which distinguishes Voter from Nonvoter for elections and commitment. The implementation bindings supply the causal path: bind-verifyleader sets v.quorumSize from quorumSize; bind-quorum counts only Voter entries; bind-startstop creates replication state for every configured non-local server; bind-notifyall and bind-heartbeat deliver a leader=true notification from any successful heartbeat; and bind-vote increments the same v.votes counter checked against quorumSize. The retained CheckRun 3c9d7e6ae7a04f4f9ce7a782e755960a executed the fixed harness in the captured snapshot and exited 0 with no build failure or changed target files. In its retained output, verify_setup is event index 0 (leader_id assurance-node-2, three voters, quorum 2, two isolated voters, one connected non-voter) and verify_outcome is event index 1 (same leader_id, operation VerifyLeader, voter_contact_count 1 from the leader itself, voter_quorum_met false, voter_confirmation_count 0, nonvoter_confirmation_count 1, result confirmed). The monitor's implication antecedent (voter_quorum_met false) and assertion (result not confirmed) evaluate false at index 1, producing a complete violating witness. The checker event, predicate fields, correlated prerequisite, and observed endpoint therefore correspond to the sourced obligation.\",\n    \"execution_attribution\": null,\n    \"report_title\": null,\n    \"report_answer\": null,\n    \"counterevidence\": [],\n    \"limitations\": [\n     \"The observation covers one three-voter/one-non-voter configuration shape and one in-memory transport schedule.\",\n     \"The harness declines the optional AppendEntriesPipeline fast path so every successful confirmation is observable through the documented fallback path.\",\n     \"The separate leader-lease timer is not part of the VerifyLeader completion endpoint observed here.\"\n    ],\n    \"challenged_components\": [],\n    \"out_of_scope_checker_ids\": []\n   },\n   {\n    \"target_id\": \"4d6db0cc9a4b4879b86886aeead58c33\",\n    \"aspect\": \"applicability\",\n    \"status\": \"no_issue_found\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n     \"src-api-verifyleader\",\n     \"src-suffrage\",\n     \"src-verifyleader\",\n     \"src-vote\",\n     \"src-notifyall\",\n     \"src-heartbeat\",\n     \"src-startstop\",\n     \"src-quorum\",\n     \"src-lease\"\n    ],\n    \"rationale\": \"The fixed sources establish the obligation's premises, and the retained execution produced them through real producers rather than a fabricated decisive state: BootstrapCluster and NewRaft created the four-node initial configuration, a committed DemoteVoter change created the three-voter/one-non-voter configuration, transport Disconnect isolated the two non-leader voters, and the real VerifyLeader API was invoked on the still-Leader node. The verify_setup event is causally before verify_outcome and shares leader_id, so the monitor correlated the admission condition with the observed result. The outcome shows the leader had only its own contact against quorum 2 and still completed confirmed. The two open applicability conditions are independent scope boundaries: the leader-lease check is a separate timer-driven mechanism after this VerifyLeader completion, and the single configuration/transport schedule limits generalization but does not change this complete witness.\",\n    \"execution_attribution\": null,\n    \"report_title\": null,\n    \"report_answer\": null,\n    \"counterevidence\": [],\n    \"limitations\": [\n     \"The result does not generalize to unobserved cluster sizes or transport implementations.\",\n     \"The result does not measure the caller-visible window before the separate lease check could step the leader down.\"\n    ],\n    \"challenged_components\": [],\n    \"