 9774e71fff2c4386b10b4cd5de50886f [src-configstore-contract,src-batchingfsm-contract,src-runfsm]: The observation covers the bootstrap configuration entry in one single-node cluster, not every configuration-change command or durable FSM implementation.; Open review issue 514044f90e6446cea1c499b51a385dc7 [src-configstore-contract,src-batchingfsm-contract,src-runfsm]: The batching branch intentionally routes LogConfiguration to ApplyBatch, but the ConfigurationStore contract independently requires StoreConfiguration for the committed configuration entry.; Open review issue 4d0f3c6b9af143cdbf76a138eabd8f6c [src-configstore-contract,src-batchingfsm-contract,src-runfsm]: The check observes the bootstrap configuration entry in one single-node cluster; it does not enumerate every configuration-change command or every durable FSM implementation.\",\n  \"trace_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-10_13-44-26-hashicorp_raft-real-run/logs/84aeffcaf772412e93f040b18483d2b5/stdout.log\",\n  \"level\": \"implementation_candidate\",\n  \"checker_id\": \"configuration_store_callback_required\",\n  \"claim_version\": 1,\n  \"applicability\": \"current\"\n }\n]\n==== evidence\n[\n {\n  \"direct_check_id\": \"4d6db0cc9a4b4879b86886aeead58c33\",\n  \"id\": \"c92498a81c0b4c08a70e5cd698ad444f\",\n  \"check_id\": \"3c9d7e6ae7a04f4f9ce7a782e755960a\",\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"a1a939b7deaa4b84a668e3a1b36a3af7\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\",\n  \"origin\": \"executed\",\n  \"level\": \"implementation_test\",\n  \"scope\": {\n   \"description\": \"A leader with a committed configuration containing both voters and at least one non-voter, a reachable transport path to the non-voter, and insufficient successful voter confirmations after VerifyLeader is admitted.\",\n   \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The mixed configuration is committed before VerifyLeader is admitted.\",\n    \"The leader is still in Leader state when VerifyLeader is admitted.\",\n    \"The non-voter can answer the verification heartbeat successfully.\"\n   ],\n   \"excluded\": [\n    \"Log commit safety and election safety under voter-only quorums.\",\n    \"Callers that do not use VerifyLeader as a read or authority guard.\",\n    \"Transports that fabricate successful responses without delivering the RPC.\"\n   ],\n   \"parameters\": {\n    \"voter_count\": 3,\n    \"nonvoter_count\": 1,\n    \"quorum_size\": 2\n   }\n  },\n  \"description\": \"Measured violated comparison; current confirmation: True\",\n  \"assessment\": \"challenged\",\n  \"stale_reason\": null,\n  \"checker_id\": \"nonvoter_cannot_complete_verify_quorum\",\n  \"claim_version\": 1,\n  \"applicability\": \"current\"\n },\n {\n  \"direct_check_id\": \"963549955e6040b89509dc7d67e601a2\",\n  \"id\": \"9cfffefc2603473eb2b0d486492780c6\",\n  \"check_id\": \"84aeffcaf772412e93f040b18483d2b5\",\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"a1a939b7deaa4b84a668e3a1b36a3af7\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-configstore-batch-callback\",\n  \"origin\": \"executed\",\n  \"level\": \"implementation_test\",\n  \"scope\": {\n   \"description\": \"One FSM value implements both ConfigurationStore and BatchingFSM, and a committed LogConfiguration entry is applied through Raft's FSM batch path.\",\n   \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The configuration entry is committed before the observation.\",\n    \"The combined FSM's ApplyBatch returns one response per received log entry.\"\n   ],\n   \"excluded\": [\n    \"FSMs that do not implement ConfigurationStore.\",\n    \"Non-configuration log entries.\",\n    \"Application-level configuration recovery outside the Raft callback contract.\"\n   ],\n   \"parameters\": {\n    \"entry_type\": \"LogConfiguration\",\n    \"batch_path\": true\n   }\n  },\n  \"description\": \"Measured violated comparison; current confirmation: False\",\n  \"assessment\": \"inconclusive\",\n  \"stale_reason\": null,\n  \"checker_id\": \"configuration_store_callback_required\",\n  \"claim_version\": 1,\n  \"applicability\": \"current\"\n }\n]\n==== units\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"unit-claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\",\n  \"candidate_id\": \"fb5c370c7acf451584b6ba19cc294a9d\",\n  \"obligation_ids\": [\n   \"claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\"\n  ],\n  \"binding_ids\": [\n   \"bind-api-verifyleader\",\n   \"bind-suffrage\",\n   \"bind-verifyleader\",\n   \"bind-vote\",\n   \"bind-notifyall\",\n   \"bind-heartbeat\",\n   \"bind-startstop\",\n   \"bind-quorum\",\n   \"bind-lease\"\n  ],\n  \"relation_ids\": [],\n  \"scope\": {\n   \"description\": \"A leader with a committed configuration containing both voters and at least one non-voter, a reachable transport path to the non-voter, and insufficient successful voter confirmations after VerifyLeader is admitted.\",\n   \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The mixed configuration is committed before VerifyLeader is admitted.\",\n    \"The leader is still in Leader state when VerifyLeader is admitted.\",\n    \"The non-voter can answer the verification heartbeat successfully.\"\n   ],\n   \"excluded\": [\n    \"Log commit safety and election safety under voter-only quorums.\",\n    \"Callers that do not use VerifyLeader as a read or authority guard.\",\n    \"Transports that fabricate successful responses without delivering the RPC.\"\n   ],\n   \"parameters\": {\n    \"voter_count\": 3,\n    \"nonvoter_count\": 1,\n    \"quorum_size\": 2\n   }\n  },\n  \"rationale\": \"The public VerifyLeader contract and the suffrage contract jointly require voter-quorum confirmation. The implementation appears to register every replication stream, including non-voters, on the same quorum-sized vote counter.\",\n  \"status\": \"checked\",\n  \"previous_id\": null,\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"boundary_changes\": [],\n  \"obligation_checks\": {\n   \"claim-verifyleader-voter-quorum-only\": [\n    \"3c9d7e6ae7a04f4f9ce7a782e755960a\"\n   ]\n  },\n  \"remaining_obligation_ids\": [],\n  \"recheck_reasons\": [],\n  \"audit_question\": {\n   \"audit_spec_version\": null,\n   \"disposition\": \"concrete_suspicion\",\n   \"preferred_check\": \"direct_test\",\n   \"question\": \"Can a leader that cannot reach a quorum of its configured voters still receive a successful VerifyLeader result because a configured non-voter answers the verification heartbeat?\",\n   \"importance\": \"VerifyLeader is documented as a guard against returning stale FSM data after leadership is lost; counting non-voter confirmations can let a separated leader confirm authority.\",\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src-api-verifyleader\",\n    \"src-suffrage\",\n    \"src-verifyleader\",\n    \"src-vote\",\n    \"src-notifyall\",\n    \"src-heartbeat\",\n    \"src-startstop\",\n    \"src-quorum\",\n    \"src-lease\"\n   ],\n   \"participants\": [],\n   \"objects\": [\n    \"VerifyLeader quorum\",\n    \"leader replication state\",\n    \"non-voter suffrage\"\n   ],\n   \"contexts\": [\n    \"leader with a committed mixed-voter configuration and a partitioned voter quorum\"\n   ],\n   \"event_paths\": [\n    \"VerifyLeader -> verifyCh -> per-replication notify -> verification heartbeat -> notifyAll -> shared vote comparison\"\n   ],\n   \"activity_classes\": [],\n   \"behavior_ids\": [],\n   \"fact_ids\": [],\n   \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {},\n   \"obligation_relation_kind\": null,\n   \"counterevidence\": [\n    \"checkLeaderLease counts only Voter entries and can step the leader down later, but that separate timer does not mediate this VerifyLeader completion.\"\n   ],\n   \"unknowns\": [\n    \"Whether the surrounding deployment uses VerifyLeader as a linearizable-read guard.\",\n    \"How long a caller may act on a false confirmation before the separate lease check fires.\"\n   ],\n   \"trigger_rationale\": \"The source binds the documented stale-read guard and the suffrage distinction directly to the observed VerifyLeader completion path.\"\n  },\n  \"coverage_limitations\": []\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"unit-claim-configstore-batch-callback\",\n  \"candidate_id\": \"e324f4661bb14b75824596f45ac3563b\",\n  \"obligation_ids\": [\n   \"claim-configstore-batch-callback\"\n  ],\n  \"binding_ids\": [\n   \"bind-configstore-contract\",\n   \"bind-batchingfsm-contract\",\n   \"bind-runfsm\"\n  ],\n  \"relation_ids\": [],\n  \"scope\": {\n   \"description\": \"One FSM value implements both ConfigurationStore and BatchingFSM, and a committed LogConfiguration entry is applied through Raft's FSM batch path.\",\n   \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The configuration entry is committed before the observation.\",\n    \"The combined FSM's ApplyBatch returns one response per received log entry.\"\n   ],\n   \"excluded\": [\n    \"FSMs that do not implement ConfigurationStore.\",\n    \"Non-configuration log entries.\",\n    \"Application-level configuration recovery outside the Raft callback contract.\"\n   ],\n   \"parameters\": {\n    \"entry_type\": \"LogConfiguration\",\n    \"batch_path\": true\n   }\n  },\n  \"rationale\": \"The ConfigurationStore interface promises StoreConfiguration once a configuration log entry is committed. The runFSM batch branch detects ConfigurationStore but sends LogConfiguration only to ApplyBatch, so a valid combined FSM can miss the promised callback.\",\n  \"status\": \"partial\",\n  \"previous_id\": null,\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"boundary_changes\": [],\n  \"obligation_checks\": {\n   \"claim-configstore-batch-callback\": [\n    \"84aeffcaf772412e93f040b18483d2b5\"\n   ]\n  },\n  \"remaining_obligation_ids\": [\n   \"claim-configstore-batch-callback\"\n  ],\n  \"recheck_reasons\": [],\n  \"audit_question\": {\n   \"audit_spec_version\": null,\n   \"disposition\": \"concrete_suspicion\",\n   \"preferred_check\": \"direct_test\",\n   \"question\": \"When an FSM implements both BatchingFSM and ConfigurationStore, is StoreConfiguration invoked for a committed configuration log entry, or is the entry only routed to ApplyBatch?\",\n   \"importance\": \"ConfigurationStore exists so a durable FSM can persist configuration changes and recover membership without an external snapshot; silently skipping the callback breaks that recovery contract for a valid FSM combination.\",\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"src-configstore-contract\",\n    \"src-batchingfsm-contract\",\n    \"src-runfsm\"\n   ],\n   \"participants\": [],\n   \"objects\": [\n    \"ConfigurationStore callback\",\n    \"BatchingFSM ApplyBatch path\",\n    \"committed LogConfiguration entry\"\n   ],\n   \"contexts\": [\n    \"one FSM value implements both optional interfaces and a committed configuration entry is applied\"\n   ],\n   \"event_paths\": [\n    \"runFSM -> batchingEnabled branch -> ApplyBatch -> no StoreConfiguration invocation\"\n   ],\n   \"activity_classes\": [],\n   \"behavior_ids\": [],\n   \"fact_ids\": [],\n   \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {},\n   \"obligation_relation_kind\": null,\n   \"counterevidence\": [\n    \"The batch branch routes LogConfiguration to ApplyBatch, which may let an application observe the entry there, but that does not satisfy the separate ConfigurationStore callback contract.\"\n   ],\n   \"unknowns\": [\n    \"Whether an affected application also reconstructs configuration through ApplyBatch or an external snapshot.\"\n   ],\n   \"trigger_rationale\": \"The interface contract and the branch structure directly determine whether StoreConfiguration is invoked for the committed configuration entry.\"\n  },\n  \"coverage_limitations\": [\n   \"Bounded direct comparison completed; local attribution remains pending: Direct oracle correspondence is unreviewed; Open review issue 39992058f9a94cb3b47c24c966810dff [src-configstore-contract,src-batchingfsm-contract,src-runfsm]: The batch branch's ApplyBatch delivery is an additional delivery path; it does not remove the separate StoreConfiguration obligation.; Open review issue 9774e71fff2c4386b10b4cd5de50886f [src-configstore-contract,src-batchingfsm-contract,src-runfsm]: The observation covers the bootstrap configuration entry in one single-node cluster, not every configuration-change command or durable FSM implementation.; Open review issue 514044f90e6446cea1c499b51a385dc7 [src-configstore-contract,src-batchingfsm-contract,src-runfsm]: The batching branch intentionally routes LogConfiguration to ApplyBatch, but the ConfigurationStore contract independently requires StoreConfiguration for the committed configuration entry.; Open review issue 4d0f3c6b9af143cdbf76a138eabd8f6c [src-configstore-contract,src-batchingfsm-contract,src-runfsm]: The check observes the bootstrap configuration entry in one single-node cluster; it does not enumerate every configuration-change command or every durable FSM implementation.\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
